## How to Chain Prompts Into a Method

To chain SEO prompts, pass reviewed evidence forward rather than treating the model's first output as fact. First group your real queries and confirm the intent. Next assign questions to existing or proposed URLs. Then create one page brief, draft or revise the page, and check facts, links and any schema before publishing. Keep the source list and unresolved questions at each handoff; this is a planning method, not a measured ranking intervention.

Pass each reviewed output to the next prompt with its supporting sources and unresolved questions. The sequence helps organise a content project; it is not a complete SEO method or evidence that the resulting pages will rank.

